# React Native

- React Native Community CLI only: no `expo`, `expo-*`, `@expo/*`, no `npx expo`.
- New Architecture and Hermes stay on; never add flags that disable them.
- Every dependency is on the allowlist in `scripts/check-deps.mjs`. A native package joins it only if:
  - its peers accept React Native 0.87 and React 19.2;
  - it supports the New Architecture;
  - it has no Expo packages in its tree;
  - both platforms build; run `npm run pods` after `npm install <package>`.
- Record new packages in the compatibility list of the guide. Ask the user before adding any package.
- Outside `src/shared/ui`, import from `react-native` only `View`, `FlatList`, `ScrollView`, `Platform`, `useWindowDimensions`, `AccessibilityInfo`; `StatusBar` only in `src/app/index.tsx`.
- UI comes from `@shared/ui`: `Typography`, `Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `StarIcon`, `RemoteImage`, `Screen`, `Loader`, `ErrorState`, `EmptyState`.
- A missing primitive is added to `src/shared/ui` as a generic component first.
- Safe areas through `SafeAreaProvider`, `Screen` and `useSafeAreaInsets`; no `SafeAreaView` from `react-native`.
- Buttons have visible text labels; favorite cards show the "In favorites" badge; touch targets use `min-h-touch` and `min-w-touch`.
- The "ImageBackground is deprecated" warning comes from `react-native-css-interop`; it is known and not suppressed. The Metro warning about `ReactNativeFeatureFlags` in `exports` comes from `@react-native/virtualized-lists`.
- `npm audit`: `braces` 3.0.3 has no patched release and reaches only build tooling, so it is accepted; `postcss-selector-parser` is raised to `^7.1.6` through `overrides`. Never `npm audit fix --force`.

Checks:
- `npm run check:deps`: allowlist and Expo scan of `package-lock.json`, part of `verify`.
- ESLint `no-restricted-imports`: visual primitives outside `src/shared/ui`, `StatusBar` outside `src/app/index.tsx`, `SafeAreaView` and `StyleSheet` everywhere.

Full guide: @docs/ai/guidelines/react-native.md
